<%= render layout: "legal_pages/page", locals: { title: "Privacy Policy", last_updated: @last_updated,
           description: "How DevBatista collects, uses and protects your personal data when you buy our digital products." } do %>
  <p>This website is operated by <strong>DevBatista Desenvolvimento de Software e Serviços LTDA</strong> ("DevBatista"), a company based in Brazil ("we", "us", "our"). We sell digital products (PDF downloads) to customers worldwide, primarily in the United States. This policy explains what personal data we collect, why, who we share it with, and the choices you have.</p>

  <h2>What we collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Purchase details:</strong> your name and email address, as provided by PayPal when you complete a purchase, plus the product bought, the amount paid and the PayPal transaction identifiers. We never see or store your card or PayPal login details.</li>
    <li><strong>Phone number (optional):</strong> only if you type it in at checkout and tick the box asking us to send your download link on WhatsApp. We store the number, the fact that you consented, the exact wording you agreed to and the date and time.</li>
    <li><strong>Technical data:</strong> IP address, browser and device information ("user agent"), the pages you visit on this site and the time of your visit.</li>
    <li><strong>Campaign data:</strong> the ad or link that brought you here (UTM parameters and click identifiers such as <code>fbclid</code>), stored in a first-party cookie so we can attribute a purchase to the campaign that generated it.</li>
    <li><strong>Support messages:</strong> anything you send us by email or WhatsApp.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Why we use it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To deliver the product you bought: we email (and, with your consent, WhatsApp) your download link, and we keep a record of the purchase so we can resend the link or issue a refund.</li>
    <li>To provide customer support and handle refunds and payment disputes.</li>
    <li>To measure and improve our advertising: we use Meta (Facebook/Instagram) Pixel and Conversions API and Google Analytics 4 to understand which ads lead to visits and purchases.</li>
    <li>To keep the site secure and prevent fraud and abuse (rate limiting, logs).</li>
    <li>To comply with legal, tax and accounting obligations.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We do <strong>not</strong> send marketing emails or messages. All emails and WhatsApp messages we send are transactional (your receipt and download link).</p>

  <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
  <p>We share personal data only with service providers that we need to run this business, each acting under its own privacy policy:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>PayPal</strong> — payment processing. PayPal collects your payment details directly.</li>
    <li><strong>Amazon Web Services (SES and S3)</strong> — sending transactional emails and storing the product files you download.</li>
    <li><strong>Twilio</strong> — sending WhatsApp messages, only if you opted in.</li>
    <li><strong>Meta Platforms</strong> and <strong>Google</strong> — advertising measurement (Meta Pixel and Conversions API, Google Analytics 4). Purchase events are sent to Meta with hashed identifiers.</li>
    <li><strong>Railway</strong> and <strong>Sentry</strong> — hosting and error monitoring.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We do not sell your personal data, and we do not share it with anyone else except when required by law or to protect our rights.</p>

  <h2>Cookies</h2>
  <p>We use a small number of cookies: a first-party cookie that remembers which campaign brought you here (kept for 30 days), a session cookie required for checkout security, and the cookies set by Meta Pixel and Google Analytics for advertising measurement. You can block or delete cookies in your browser settings; the site and checkout will still work. You can also opt out of Meta and Google ad measurement through their own tools (Meta ad preferences and the Google Analytics opt-out browser add-on).</p>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>Purchase records (name, email, product, amount, transaction identifiers) are kept for as long as required for tax, accounting and dispute purposes — typically 5 years. Download links expire after a short period, but you can request a new one at any time. Technical logs are kept for up to 90 days. If you asked us to delete your data, we keep only what the law requires us to retain.</p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>You can ask us to tell you what personal data we hold about you, correct it, or delete it. Email <a href="mailto:<%= support_email %>"><%= support_email %></a> from the address you used at checkout and we will respond within 30 days. Deleting your purchase record means we can no longer resend your download link.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>California residents (CCPA/CPRA):</strong> you have the right to know, delete and correct your personal information and to opt out of its "sale" or "sharing". We do not sell personal information. Advertising measurement through Meta and Google may be considered "sharing" under California law; you can opt out by blocking their cookies as described above or by emailing us. We will not discriminate against you for exercising these rights.</li>
    <li><strong>Brazil (LGPD):</strong> as a Brazilian operator we process data under the Lei Geral de Proteção de Dados. You may exercise the rights in Article 18 (confirmation, access, correction, anonymization, deletion, portability and information about sharing) by contacting us at the address above.</li>
    <li><strong>Other regions:</strong> if your local law grants you additional rights, you can exercise them the same way.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Security</h2>
  <p>Data is transmitted over HTTPS and stored with providers that maintain industry-standard security. Product files are kept in private storage and are only reachable through temporary, signed links. No method of transmission or storage is completely secure, but we take reasonable steps to protect your data.</p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>Our products are intended for adults. We do not knowingly collect data from anyone under 16. If you believe a minor has made a purchase, contact us and we will delete the data and refund the purchase.</p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>We may update this policy from time to time. The date at the top shows when it was last changed. Continued use of the site after a change means you accept the updated policy.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>DevBatista Desenvolvimento de Software e Serviços LTDA — <a href="mailto:<%= support_email %>"><%= support_email %></a></p>
<% end %>
